    "faq": {
      "type": "vk-faq",
      "settings": {
        "layout": "split",
        "index": "09",
        "eyebrow": "FAQ",
        "heading": "Questions, <em>answered</em>.",
        "subheading": "Everything worth knowing before your first sear.",
        "show_filter": true,
        "contact_title": "Still curious?",
        "contact_text": "Talk to a person — we reply within one working day.",
        "contact_url": "/pages/contact",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "padding_top": 120,
        "padding_bottom": 120
      },
      "blocks": {
        "question-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is VOLKARA safe? Is it really PFAS-free?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. VOLKARA cookware contains no PFAS, PTFE or PFOA and has no synthetic coating of any kind. Your food touches titanium — a non-reactive metal that doesn't alter flavour — bonded to stainless steel. Test reports are available on request.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will food stick? How do I cook on it?",
            "answer": "<p>It isn't a coated pan, so technique matters for the first few cooks. Preheat on medium for two to three minutes, until a drop of water skates across the surface. Add a thin film of oil, let it shimmer, add your food and leave it until it releases on its own. If something sticks, the pan wasn't quite hot enough or the food moved too soon — and it soaks off in minutes.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use metal utensils?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The raised LavaCell™ peaks take the contact and protect the titanium in the valleys, so spatulas, whisks and tongs are welcome. Over the years the peaks develop a soft polish. That's patina, not damage, and it doesn't affect performance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which heat sources does it work on?",
            "answer": "<p>All of them: gas, induction, ceramic, electric, halogen, oven and grill. The magnetic 18/0 steel base sits flat on induction. On gas, keep the flame within the base for the most even heat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it dishwasher-safe?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — there is no coating for a dishwasher to strip. We still suggest warm water and a soft sponge: it's quicker and keeps the exterior brilliant. For stubborn residue, simmer a little water for a minute, then wipe.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How hot can it go in the oven?",
            "answer": "<p>Pans and pots are oven- and grill-safe to 260°C. Tempered glass lids are oven-safe to 180°C. Handles get hot in the oven, so always use a cloth or glove.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the lifetime warranty cover?",
            "answer": "<p>Every VolcanicCore™ piece is guaranteed against defects in materials and workmanship for its lifetime in household use — including delamination, warping under normal use and handle failure. It doesn't cover cosmetic wear, misuse or commercial kitchens. The warranty comes on top of your statutory rights, which are never affected. Full terms on our <a href=\"/pages/warranty\">warranty page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the 60-day home trial work?",
            "answer": "<p>Cook with it for up to 60 days from delivery. If it isn't the best pan you own, tell us, send it back clean and complete, and we'll refund the purchase price. Used is fine. Your statutory 14-day right of withdrawal applies separately.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How fast is shipping, and what does it cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Orders are dispatched within one to two working days and usually arrive within two to five. Shipping is free on orders over €75; below that, the rate is shown at checkout before you pay. You'll receive a tracking link the moment your order leaves us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to season it?",
            "answer": "<p>No. VOLKARA works straight from the box after a wash. If you like, give it a two-minute activation: warm the pan, wipe in a teaspoon of neutral oil, heat until it shimmers, cool and wipe. There's no ongoing seasoning ritual like cast iron.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How heavy is it?",
            "answer": "<p>Balanced rather than heavy. The 28 cm Forge Pan weighs about 1.3 kg — more than a thin coated pan, far less than cast iron of the same size. The forged handle places the weight where your wrist expects it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is it different from other hammered titanium or hybrid pans?",
            "answer": "<p>Many \"titanium\" and hybrid pans are stainless steel with a coating in disguise — a raised steel pattern filled with non-stick, or a titanium-reinforced coating that still wears away. VolcanicCore™ has no coating at all: the cooking surface is titanium, laser-etched into a LavaCell™ relief and bonded into a five-layer forged body. Nothing to wear through, no hidden fluoropolymer, and a lifetime warranty in writing.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
